### MAMGA Memory MCP (auto-wired — always use)
At the START of EVERY session:
1. Call `get_recent_memory` (mamga-memory MCP) → restore last session context
2. Call `list_sessions` → show recent session IDs
3. Report: "Memory restored: [N] recent memories loaded"

During session — after completing any significant task:
1. Call `store_memory` with what was learned/decided
2. Include: project context, decisions made, patterns observed

At the END of every session:
1. Call `store_memory` with session summary
2. Extract coding patterns → save as instincts to:
   `C:\Users\I075354\.claude\homunculus\projects\<hash>\instincts\personal\`
3. Report: "Session saved. Use /instinct-status to review."

### Memory MCP Tools (mamga-memory server)
- `store_memory`         → persist a learning/decision
- `query_memory`         → search past memories by topic
- `get_recent_memory`    → restore last N session memories
- `get_session_summary`  → summarize a past session
- `list_sessions`        → show all session IDs

### Memory Commands (type in Cline chat)
- `/learn`            → extract patterns from current session NOW
- `/instinct-status`  → show learned instincts with confidence
- `/evolve`           → cluster instincts into reusable skills
- `/instinct-export`  → export memory backup

