## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════
## HOOK 3: E2E UI TESTING (Playwright + Chrome DevTools MCP)
## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════
## AUTO-TRIGGER: "test UI", "click test", "console spy", "E2E", "browser"
## BEHAVIOR: Generate Playwright tests with console spy + Chrome DevTools live inspection

### Chrome DevTools MCPs (auto-wired — 2 servers)
- `chrome-devtools`  → chrome-devtools-mcp@latest --autoConnect --channel=beta
- `devtools-mcp`     → @chrome-devtools/mcp@latest

USE for:
- Console spy: capture console.log/error/warn from live browser
- Network spy: monitor API calls, responses, 4xx/5xx errors
- DOM: inspect element visibility, attributes, computed styles
- Performance: page load, paint, memory metrics
- Screenshot: capture browser state at any moment

### Auto-Generated E2E Template (ALWAYS use this pattern)
```typescript
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test'

test.describe('[Feature Name]', () => {
  const consoleLogs: string[] = []
  const consoleErrors: string[] = []

  test.beforeEach(async ({ page }) => {
    // Wire console spy BEFORE navigation
    page.on('console', msg => {
      if (msg.type() === 'error') consoleErrors.push(msg.text())
      else consoleLogs.push(`[${msg.type()}] ${msg.text()}`)
    })
    // Wire network spy
    page.on('response', resp => {
      if (resp.status() >= 400)
        console.warn(`[NetworkError] ${resp.status()} ${resp.url()}`)
    })
    await page.goto('/your-url')
    await page.waitForLoadState('networkidle')
  })

  test.afterEach(async () => {
    // Assert no console errors automatically
    expect(consoleErrors, `Console errors found: ${consoleErrors.join('; ')}`).toHaveLength(0)
  })

  test('should handle click', async ({ page }) => {
    await page.locator('[data-testid="your-button"]').click()
    await expect(page.locator('[data-testid="result"]')).toBeVisible()
    await page.screenshot({ path: 'artifacts/after-click.png' })
  })
})
```

### E2E Commands
- `/e2e`           → generate E2E tests with console+network spy
- `/tdd`           → TDD: write tests first, then implement
- `/verify`        → run verification loop
- `/test-coverage` → check % coverage

## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════
## PLANDB — TASK CONTROLLER (HARD RULE for multi-step tasks) before context window reach limit
## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════
## Script: C:\AI\autoresearch\scripts\plandb.py
## Global cmd: plandb (on PATH via plandb.bat)
## DB: C:\AI\autoresearch\.plandb.sqlite (auto-created)
##
## PURPOSE: Prevent tool-loop failures shown as:
##   This may indicate a failure in Clines thought process
## ROOT CAUSE: Chaining 3+ tool calls without checkpoints.
## SOLUTION: Each plandb task = exactly ONE primary tool call.

STEP 1 - SESSION START (always first):
  python C:\AI\autoresearch\scripts\plandb.py status
  - in_progress: resume, do NOT add duplicates
  - all done/empty: proceed to add new steps

STEP 2 - DECOMPOSE upfront (ALL steps before ANY work):
  plandb add step-1-title
  plandb add step-2-title
  Add ALL steps first. Never add-as-you-go.

STEP 3 - CLAIM: plandb go  (do ONLY that one step)
STEP 4 - ADVANCE: plandb done --next  (then do next step)
STEP 5 - CONFIRM: plandb list  (all must show done)

RULE A - ONE TOOL CALL PER PLANDB STEP. Need 2 calls = 2 tasks.
RULE B - NEVER RETRY SAME TOOL 3+ TIMES. Fail = replan via plandb.
RULE C - NEVER write_file FOR .js SCRIPTS. Use node -e inline instead.
RULE D - NEVER CHAIN TOOLS without plandb checkpoints between them.
RULE E - WHEN BLOCKED: plandb list BEFORE asking user.
RULE F - NEVER ASK PERMISSION FOR PLANDB. 2+ steps = use it auto.
RULE G - NEVER LEAVE in_progress ACROSS SESSIONS. Resume next session.
RULE H - TOOL FAILURE WARNING = STOP, run plandb status, replan now.

QUICK REF: plandb status / add / go / done --next / list

