## RULE 11 - Coding Artifacts Must Stay in Their Original Project Folder
## WARNING: HARD RULE - NON-NEGOTIABLE - OVERRIDES ALL CONVENIENCE
## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════

PRINCIPLE: Every artifact lives exactly where it belongs.
VIOLATION: Work must be redone in the correct location. No exceptions.

11.1 - Scratch / Compose / Temp Work -> tmp/
  Exploratory/spike code         -> tmp/auth-spike-20260507.ts
  Draft snippets                 -> tmp/draft-parser-20260507.py
  One-off migration scripts      -> tmp/migrate-once-20260507.sh
  Quick proof-of-concept         -> tmp/poc-caching-20260507.ts
  Temp test iterations           -> tmp/feature-x-draft-20260507.test.ts
  Experiments                    -> tmp/try-new-algo-20260507.py
  Screenshot artifacts           -> tmp/after-click-20260507.png
  Naming convention: tmp/<short-description>-<YYYYMMDD>.<ext>

  tmp/ rules:
  - git-ignored (already in .gitignore)
  - NEVER imported by production code
  - NEVER committed
  - Safe to delete entire tmp/ at any time
  - Research docs go in research/ or docs/ NOT tmp/

11.2 - Test Files: Draft in tmp/, Promote When Stable
  tmp/my-feature-test-20260507.test.ts  <- iterate freely
  |  once stable + passing
  v
  tests/my-feature.test.ts               <- promoted, lint-clean, committed
  Promoted tests MUST pass lint before commit.

11.3 - Production / Useful Code -> Original Project Location
  - All shipped code MUST reside in canonical project location
  - No production logic in tmp/
  - No stray files in project root
  - Run lint before committing to final location

11.4 - Cross-Project Contamination is Forbidden
  - Code for project A must NEVER go into project B folder
  - NEVER create autoresearch/ subfolders inside this project
  - NEVER create this project subfolders inside autoresearch/

11.5 - Folder Ownership Map (this project)
  Scratch/spikes/drafts       tmp/
  Temp test drafts            tmp/
  Stable tests (promoted)     tests/ or src/__tests__/
  Source code                 src/ or appropriate subdir
  Agents                      agents/
  Commands                    commands/
  Hooks                       hooks/
  Skills                      skills/
  Documentation               docs/
  Research outputs            research/
  Scripts                     scripts/
  Schema definitions          schemas/
  Examples                    examples/

11.6 - Pre-Write Checklist (run mentally before every write_file):
  [ ] Scratch/exploratory?   -> tmp/
  [ ] Temp test?             -> tmp/, promote when stable
  [ ] Production code?       -> correct src/ location then lint
  [ ] Different project?     -> write there not here
  [ ] Being committed?       -> must pass lint first

## =================================================
## RULE 12 - OpenClaw Memory Architecture (Added 2026-05-05)
## =================================================
Read memory files BEFORE any work. Maintain them AFTER work.

Memory layers:
  Layer 01 Identity:   IDENTITY.md, SOUL.md, USER.md
  Layer 02 Long-Term:  MEMORY.md
  Layer 03 Working:    memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md (one per day, append-only)
  Layer 04 Operations: AGENTS.md, TOOLS.md, HEARTBEAT.md

SESSION START - read before any work:
  1. Read IDENTITY.md
  2. Read SOUL.md
  3. Read USER.md
  4. Read MEMORY.md
  5. Check memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md (Asia/Shanghai date):
     - NOT exists: CREATE it with session-start entry
     - EXISTS: read fully then APPEND session-start note
  6. python C:\AI\autoresearch\scripts\plandb.py status

DURING WORK:
  - Make minimal safe edits - inspect before modifying
  - Track important decisions in memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md
  - Use PlanDB for all multi-step tasks - no exceptions

SESSION END:
  - Append session-end summary to memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md
  - Promote ONLY stable durable facts to MEMORY.md
  - Mark all completed plandb tasks done

Daily memory file: memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md (append-only, auto-created)

## =================================================
## RULE 13 - CF Deploy Verification (HARD RULE - NO EXCEPTIONS)
## =================================================
After ANY CF deployment (cf push, cf restart, cf start):

MANDATORY verification pattern (replace APP_NAME with actual app):
  Step 1: cf app APP_NAME
           -> read instances: must show 1/1 (not 0/1)
  Step 3: curl.exe -v https://APP_URL/health
           -> must return HTTP 200

PASS criteria: instances 1/1 AND curl returns HTTP 200
FAIL criteria: instances 0/1 OR curl returns 4xx/5xx -> fix and redeploy

HALLUCINATION TRAPS - NEVER:
  - NEVER report web:1/1 from memory - run cf app NAME and read NEW output NOW
  - NEVER reuse old cf app output from a previous message
  - NEVER report HTTP 200 without curl output appearing in THIS response
  - NEVER mark task done if cf app shows web:0/1
  - NEVER hardcode app URLs in rules - derive from cf app output each time

## =================================================
## GENERAL CODE QUALITY (auto-enforce on every file edit)
## =================================================

- Always add data-testid to interactive UI elements (enables E2E)
- Never commit console.log without // TODO: remove comment
- TypeScript: strict mode always
- Validate all inputs, never trust external data
- Use Path(__file__).parent for CF-deployed Python asset paths
- BTP CF: pass env vars explicitly via subprocess env dict

Lint Gate (MUST pass before committing outside tmp/):
  npm run lint   OR  eslint <file>
  prettier --check <file>  OR  npm run format:check
  Python: ruff check + black --check
  Rust:   cargo clippy + cargo fmt --check
  Zero tolerance for lint failures on committed code.

Security:
- Never hardcode secrets, API keys, tokens, credentials
- Use environment variables for all configuration
- SAP: use XSUAA OAuth tokens, never bypass auth
- No magic numbers without named constants + comment

Git:
- Conventional commits: feat/fix/chore/docs/test/refactor
- Keep commits small and focused
- Body must explain WHY not just WHAT

