## =================================================
## CLINE RECOVERY AND RESUME RULES (Added 2026-05-08)
## =================================================

When resuming a task after an error:
1. Do not blindly retry the failed operation.
2. First summarize the last known goal.
3. Identify the exact error.
4. Continue from the last safe step.
5. If the error is provider/model/API related, do not retry until configuration is corrected.
6. If the error is a malformed tool call, regenerate the tool call with correct required parameters.
7. If the same error appears twice, stop and ask the user.

## =================================================
## LITELLM RULES (Added 2026-05-08)
## =================================================

Never blindly retry LiteLLM 400 errors.

A LiteLLM 400 error usually means:
- wrong model name
- wrong provider
- wrong base URL
- wrong API key
- unsupported model
- invalid proxy mapping
- bad request format

If a LiteLLM 400 error happens:
1. Stop.
2. Print the modelId and providerId.
3. Ask the user to confirm the correct model alias.
4. Do not retry the same modelId.

## =================================================
## EXECUTE_COMMAND APPROVAL RULES (Added 2026-05-08)
## =================================================

Every execute_command call MUST include requires_approval. Never omit it.

Safe read-only commands -> requires_approval=false:
  pwd, ls, cat, grep, find, git status,
  python --version, node --version, npm test, pytest

System-modifying commands -> requires_approval=true:
  npm install, pip install, rm, mv, cp,
  git reset, git clean, git push, docker,
  database migration, chmod, chown,
  curl pipe to shell, wget pipe to shell
